\title{Amortized cost of ZIG-ZIG}
\date{2026-11-25T22:44:00Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Lemma}
\p{The amortized cost of a [\strong{ZIG-ZIG} operation](00UI) is #{\leq 3(R'(x) -
  R(x))}.}

\proof{
The actual cost of \strong{ZIG-ZIG} is #{2} rotations; the only nodes whose ranks change are #{x}, #{p}, and #{g}. So the amortized cost is

    \stmt{#{2 + R'(g) - R(g) + R'(p) - R(p) + R'(x) - R(x)}}
    \reason{=}{#{R(g) = R'(x)}}
    \stmt{#{2 + R'(g) + R'(p) - R(p) - R(x)}}
    \reason{#{<}}{#{R(x) < R(p)}, so #{-R(p) < -R(x)}}
    \stmt{#{2 + R'(g) + R'(p) - 2R(x)}}
    \reason{#{<}}{#{R'(p) < R'(x)}}
    \stmt{#{2 + R'(g) + R'(x) - 2R(x)}}
    \reason{#{\leq}}{[[00UK]]}
    \stmt{#{(2R'(x) -  R(x) - R'(g)) + R'(g) + R'(x) - 2R(x)}}
    \reason{=}{algebra}
    \stmt{#{3(R'(x) - R(x))}.}
}
